## Disable Intelligence write CTAs in read-only mode

Context: On a read-only domain (no edit rights, non-DRAFT version, or
Resume editing / another editor's lock), Patterns New, Communities Clear
graph and Scenarios New stayed clickable because they were missing from
``permissions.css``. The async edit-lock flip lands after page JS has
already synced ``_canEdit``, so CSS gates are required.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/css/permissions.css
   Gate ``#patDetectBtn``, ``#patDetectRunBtn``, ``#commClearBtn``,
   ``#commDetectBtn``, ``#commMaterializeBtn``, ``#simNewBtn`` under
   ``body:is(.read-only-version, .role-viewer, .read-only-locked)``.
2. src/front/static/intelligence/js/simulation.js
   ``_canEdit`` / ``_applyEditGate`` for New scenario; refuse
   ``newScenario`` with a read-only toast.
3. tests/units/front/test_view_mode_write_gates.py
   Contract for the CSS gates and the Scenarios JS guard.

